<h2> Ancient China: Dynasties and Early Civilization Systems</h2>
<h3> WELL DETAILED NOTES</h3>

<p>
Ancient China was one of the world’s longest-lasting and most influential civilizations. It developed primarily around the <b>Yellow River (Huang He)</b> and later expanded across large regions of East Asia.
</p>

<p>
Unlike civilizations that disappeared completely after collapse,
Chinese civilization repeatedly rebuilt itself through a pattern known as the:
</p>

<p>
<b>Dynastic Cycle</b>
</p>

