</li>

<li>
It explored ethics, consciousness, and human behavior.
</li>

<li>
They were often integrated into one knowledge system.
</li>

<li>
Mathematics, astronomy, medicine, philosophy, and logic.
</li>

<li>
Through trade, scholarship, and cultural exchange.
</li>

<li>
That true advancement includes both external systems and internal understanding.
</li>

<li>
Because its ideas still influence mathematics, philosophy, medicine, and psychology today.
</li>

</ol>
